  "notes": "- First-person hands redone on every gun, set by hand gun by gun: real-size hands (they were far too big,\n  which swallowed the handguns and SMGs), the right hand wrapped round the grip with a finger on the trigger\n  and the thumb round the far side, the left hand under the handguard with its fingers curled up the far side.\n  Handguns get a proper two-handed grip; shotguns and bolt rifles hold the wrist of the stock; vertical grips\n  (the attachment, and the Strix's and Vortex's own) are wrapped properly. Thumbs no longer stick out.\n- Drawing tablet support (Settings: Drawing Tablet (Pen Aims)): the pen aims and tapping shoots. Lifting\n  the pen and putting it down elsewhere doesn't jerk the view; hold it at the left or right edge to keep\n  turning. Mouse Sensitivity sets the speed.",
